1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,434
Late August, 2019.

2
00:00:02,434 --> 00:00:06,019
In an industrial area of Tijuana, Mexican law

3
00:00:06,019 --> 00:00:09,365
enforcement find the entrance to a tunnel,

4
00:00:09,365 --> 00:00:12,392
hidden by a small industrial building.

5
00:00:12,842 --> 00:00:16,386
About 70 feet below the surface, it runs north.

6
00:00:16,386 --> 00:00:17,668
Under the border.

7
00:00:17,668 --> 00:00:20,759
Into the warehouse district of Otay Mesa,

8
00:00:20,759 --> 00:00:21,589
California.

9
00:00:22,039 --> 00:00:25,123
It has a rail system, forced-air ventilation,

10
00:00:25,123 --> 00:00:28,208
high-voltage power cables, a drainage system,

11
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:30,401
and an elevator at the entrance.

12
00:00:30,851 --> 00:00:34,034
When the task force finishes mapping it, it

13
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,514
measures 4,309 feet.

14
00:00:35,514 --> 00:00:38,105
More than three quarters of a mile.

15
00:00:38,555 --> 00:00:41,448
The longest smuggling tunnel ever found along

16
00:00:41,448 --> 00:00:41,963
the U.S.

17
00:00:41,963 --> 00:00:43,056
southwest border.

18
00:00:43,506 --> 00:00:45,534
There are no arrests. No drugs.

19
00:00:45,534 --> 00:00:47,628
So who digs something like this?

20
00:00:47,628 --> 00:00:50,442
And how do you find a tunnel buried 70 feet

21
00:00:50,442 --> 00:00:51,293
under a city?

22
00:00:51,893 --> 00:00:54,858
This is the story of the tunnels under the border.

23
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:01,533
The modern tunnel era begins in Arizona, in 1990.

24
00:01:01,983 --> 00:01:05,160
In May of that year, investigators uncover a

25
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:08,265
tunnel running from a house in Agua Prieta,

26
00:01:08,265 --> 00:01:11,369
Mexico, to a warehouse in Douglas, Arizona.

27
00:01:11,819 --> 00:01:13,902
It's only about 200 feet long.

28
00:01:13,902 --> 00:01:16,609
But it's lined with concrete, wired for

29
00:01:16,609 --> 00:01:19,594
electricity, and equipped with drains and a

30
00:01:19,594 --> 00:01:20,566
pulley system.

31
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:23,815
The entrance on the Mexican side is hidden

32
00:01:23,815 --> 00:01:25,082
under a pool table.

33
00:01:25,082 --> 00:01:27,948
When someone turns on an outdoor water tap,

34
00:01:27,948 --> 00:01:31,213
hydraulics raise a section of the concrete floor.

35
00:01:31,663 --> 00:01:34,836
The tunnel is linked to the organization of a

36
00:01:34,836 --> 00:01:36,669
rising Sinaloa trafficker.

37
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:39,066
Joaquín Guzmán, known as El Chapo.

38
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:42,956
The architect who oversaw its construction,

39
00:01:42,956 --> 00:01:46,396
Felipe de Jesús Corona-Verbera, spends more

40
00:01:46,396 --> 00:01:48,396
than a decade on the run.

41
00:01:48,396 --> 00:01:51,996
He's arrested in 2003, convicted in Tucson in

42
00:01:51,996 --> 00:01:54,556
2006, and sentenced to 18 years.

43
00:01:55,006 --> 00:01:57,569
By then, the idea had spread.

44
00:01:57,569 --> 00:01:59,955
Between 1990 and 2011, U.S.

45
00:01:59,955 --> 00:02:03,402
authorities found 149 tunnels under the

46
00:02:03,402 --> 00:02:04,905
southwest border.

47
00:02:05,355 --> 00:02:07,252
Most of them in two states.

48
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:08,939
Arizona, and California.

49
00:02:09,939 --> 00:02:12,435
Not every tunnel is a feat of engineering.

50
00:02:12,885 --> 00:02:16,005
In Nogales, Arizona, smugglers dig into the

51
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:18,908
city's storm drains, which run under the

52
00:02:18,908 --> 00:02:20,287
border into Mexico.

53
00:02:20,737 --> 00:02:25,324
By August 2015, Border Patrol's Tucson Sector

54
00:02:25,324 --> 00:02:27,566
had found 113 tunnels.

55
00:02:27,566 --> 00:02:29,911
107 of them in Nogales.

56
00:02:30,361 --> 00:02:31,341
Many are crude.

57
00:02:31,341 --> 00:02:34,284
Narrow holes, dug by hand, barely wide enough

58
00:02:34,284 --> 00:02:35,395
to crawl through.

59
00:02:35,845 --> 00:02:37,841
But a few are something else.

60
00:02:37,841 --> 00:02:41,281
Long, deep, lit, ventilated and fitted with rails.

61
00:02:41,281 --> 00:02:44,170
Officials call them sophisticated tunnels.

62
00:02:44,170 --> 00:02:46,853
And most of those turn up in one place.

63
00:02:47,303 --> 00:02:50,567
Otay Mesa, on the southern edge of San Diego.

64
00:02:51,017 --> 00:02:54,154
Here, industrial parks sit on both sides of

65
00:02:54,154 --> 00:02:54,956
the border.

66
00:02:54,956 --> 00:02:58,676
Warehouses in Tijuana face warehouses in San Diego.

67
00:02:59,126 --> 00:03:02,233
The DEA says the terrain here is easier to dig.

68
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:04,414
And the warehouses provide cover.

69
00:03:04,414 --> 00:03:07,851
Thousands of commercial trucks cross here every day.

70
00:03:08,301 --> 00:03:10,451
So the business model is simple.

71
00:03:10,451 --> 00:03:12,466
Dig from a building in Mexico.

72
00:03:12,466 --> 00:03:14,952
Come up inside a building in the U S.

73
00:03:14,952 --> 00:03:17,639
Load the drugs onto trucks, and let them

74
00:03:17,639 --> 00:03:19,587
vanish into ordinary traffic.

75
00:03:20,587 --> 00:03:24,405
San Diego's answer is a dedicated tunnel task force.

76
00:03:24,855 --> 00:03:26,331
It's formed in 2003.

77
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:29,283
Homeland Security Investigations, Border

78
00:03:29,283 --> 00:03:32,530
Patrol, the DEA, and state narcotics agents.

79
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:35,408
They work with electronic surveillance,

80
00:03:35,408 --> 00:03:38,803
old-fashioned detective work and tips from the

81
00:03:38,803 --> 00:03:39,319
public.

82
00:03:39,769 --> 00:03:43,801
In November 2010, they hit two tunnels in one month.

83
00:03:44,251 --> 00:03:45,627
In the first, U.S.

84
00:03:45,627 --> 00:03:48,226
agents seize 20 tons of marijuana.

85
00:03:48,226 --> 00:03:52,123
Mexican soldiers seize 4.5 tons more on their side.

86
00:03:52,573 --> 00:03:55,358
On Thanksgiving, they find the second.

87
00:03:55,358 --> 00:03:58,583
Nearly half a mile long, about 90 feet deep,

88
00:03:58,583 --> 00:04:01,661
with two exits in the U S, 800 feet apart.

89
00:04:02,111 --> 00:04:05,055
On the Mexican side, the shaft drops through a

90
00:04:05,055 --> 00:04:05,951
kitchen floor.

91
00:04:05,951 --> 00:04:08,319
Inside, there are rails, electricity,

92
00:04:08,319 --> 00:04:09,791
ventilation and lights.

93
00:04:10,241 --> 00:04:13,338
About 20 tons of marijuana are seized on both

94
00:04:13,338 --> 00:04:14,715
sides of the border.

95
00:04:14,715 --> 00:04:18,156
Eight people are arrested, five of them in Mexico.

96
00:04:18,606 --> 00:04:21,053
A year later, it happens again.

97
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:24,604
In November 2011, a tunnel of about 600 yards

98
00:04:24,604 --> 00:04:26,262
links two warehouses.

99
00:04:26,262 --> 00:04:29,971
Electric rail cars, lighting, reinforced walls.

100
00:04:29,971 --> 00:04:33,365
On the Mexican side, a hydraulic steel door

101
00:04:33,365 --> 00:04:34,627
and an elevator.

102
00:04:35,077 --> 00:04:38,238
Agents seize more than 32 tons of marijuana.

103
00:04:38,238 --> 00:04:39,963
Six people are arrested.

104
00:04:40,413 --> 00:04:43,049
Prosecutors charge a man ICE calls a

105
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:46,272
high-ranking operative of the Sinaloa cartel

106
00:04:46,272 --> 00:04:49,495
with running the Thanksgiving tunnel and the

107
00:04:49,495 --> 00:04:50,374
2011 tunnel.

108
00:04:50,374 --> 00:04:53,597
The press calls him the Lord of the Tunnels.

109
00:04:54,047 --> 00:04:57,538
José Sánchez Villalobos is extradited from

110
00:04:57,538 --> 00:04:58,785
Mexico in 2020.

111
00:04:58,785 --> 00:05:02,360
He pleads guilty, and in 2021, according to

112
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,769
press reports, he's sentenced to about 10

113
00:05:05,769 --> 00:05:07,764
years in federal prison.

114
00:05:08,764 --> 00:05:12,076
For years, the tunnels mostly carried one thing.

115
00:05:12,076 --> 00:05:12,766
Marijuana.

116
00:05:12,766 --> 00:05:14,353
Then the cargo changes.

117
00:05:14,803 --> 00:05:18,438
On October 30, 2013, agents shut down a tunnel

118
00:05:18,438 --> 00:05:22,073
about six football fields long, with lighting,

119
00:05:22,073 --> 00:05:24,681
ventilation and an electric rail.

120
00:05:25,131 --> 00:05:28,603
They seize more than 8 tons of marijuana.

121
00:05:28,603 --> 00:05:30,805
And 325 pounds of cocaine.

122
00:05:31,255 --> 00:05:33,781
It's the first cocaine ever recovered in

123
00:05:33,781 --> 00:05:35,991
connection with a San Diego tunnel.

124
00:05:36,441 --> 00:05:40,045
In April 2014, agents find two more tunnels in

125
00:05:40,045 --> 00:05:40,828
four days.

126
00:05:40,828 --> 00:05:44,275
On camera, agents scan a warehouse floor and

127
00:05:44,275 --> 00:05:46,233
cut through the concrete.

128
00:05:46,683 --> 00:05:47,212
The U.S.

129
00:05:47,212 --> 00:05:49,656
attorney in San Diego puts it simply.

130
00:05:49,656 --> 00:05:52,827
“Going underground is not a good business plan.”

131
00:05:53,277 --> 00:05:57,199
In March 2016, the tunnel ends under a newly

132
00:05:57,199 --> 00:06:00,408
built house in Calexico, California.

133
00:06:00,408 --> 00:06:04,776
It runs 415 yards, from a restaurant in Mexicali.

134
00:06:05,226 --> 00:06:08,661
Agents seize nearly 3,000 pounds of marijuana.

135
00:06:09,111 --> 00:06:12,535
A month later, back in Otay Mesa, they find a

136
00:06:12,535 --> 00:06:15,808
zigzagging tunnel more than 800 yards long,

137
00:06:15,808 --> 00:06:17,710
only about 3 feet across.

138
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:20,982
In Tijuana, it starts with a large elevator

139
00:06:20,982 --> 00:06:22,124
inside a house.

140
00:06:22,574 --> 00:06:26,775
This time, agents seize 2,242 pounds of cocaine.

141
00:06:26,775 --> 00:06:30,451
The largest cocaine seizure ever tied to a

142
00:06:30,451 --> 00:06:32,814
Southern California tunnel.

143
00:06:33,264 --> 00:06:35,980
The DEA puts the change in one sentence.

144
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:39,104
“Historically, seizures from drug tunnels have

145
00:06:39,104 --> 00:06:42,160
been marijuana and small amounts of cocaine.”

146
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:45,889
And not every tunnel ends in a warehouse.

147
00:06:45,889 --> 00:06:49,007
In August 2018, in San Luis, Arizona, a

148
00:06:49,007 --> 00:06:52,046
traffic stop turns up methamphetamine,

149
00:06:52,046 --> 00:06:54,365
fentanyl, heroin and cocaine.

150
00:06:54,815 --> 00:06:58,237
It leads investigators to a tunnel nearly 600

151
00:06:58,237 --> 00:06:58,998
feet long.

152
00:06:58,998 --> 00:07:02,268
It starts under a bed in a house in Mexico,

153
00:07:02,268 --> 00:07:05,311
and ends in the kitchen of a former KFC.

154
00:07:06,311 --> 00:07:08,460
Which brings us back to the tunnel from the

155
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:09,660
beginning of this story.

156
00:07:10,110 --> 00:07:13,493
Its entrance is in Tijuana, about half a mile

157
00:07:13,493 --> 00:07:16,200
west of the Otay Mesa port of entry.

158
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:19,132
A task force of the DEA, Border Patrol,

159
00:07:19,132 --> 00:07:22,440
Homeland Security Investigations and federal

160
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,598
prosecutors maps it from the Mexican side.

161
00:07:26,048 --> 00:07:28,979
Border Patrol's official footage calls it the

162
00:07:28,979 --> 00:07:29,696
Baja Metro.

163
00:07:30,146 --> 00:07:33,613
On average, it runs 70 feet underground.

164
00:07:33,613 --> 00:07:37,686
It's about 5.5 feet tall, and just 2 feet wide.

165
00:07:37,686 --> 00:07:41,239
4,068 feet of it lie north of the border.

166
00:07:41,689 --> 00:07:44,918
About 3,500 feet into the U S, a short branch

167
00:07:44,918 --> 00:07:47,429
stops without reaching the surface.

168
00:07:47,429 --> 00:07:50,585
The main tunnel keeps going, roughly another

169
00:07:50,585 --> 00:07:54,316
city block, to what agents believe was its old exit.

170
00:07:54,316 --> 00:07:57,903
It had been blocked with several hundred sandbags.

171
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:02,248
The previous record, found in San Diego in

172
00:08:02,248 --> 00:08:04,196
2014, was 2,966 feet.

173
00:08:04,196 --> 00:08:08,369
The Baja Metro beat it by more than a quarter

174
00:08:08,369 --> 00:08:09,297
of a mile.

175
00:08:09,747 --> 00:08:12,583
Agents who go inside wear air monitors.

176
00:08:12,583 --> 00:08:14,910
In this tunnel, the alarm beeps.

177
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:16,509
Oxygen is running low.

178
00:08:16,959 --> 00:08:19,920
The DEA's special agent in charge says the

179
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:23,022
tunnel shows the determination and the money

180
00:08:23,022 --> 00:08:24,362
behind the cartels.

181
00:08:24,812 --> 00:08:27,139
There were no arrests and no seizures.

182
00:08:27,139 --> 00:08:29,710
And as far as officials have reported, the

183
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:30,935
record still stands.

184
00:08:31,935 --> 00:08:34,089
Finding these tunnels is still hard.

185
00:08:34,539 --> 00:08:37,106
The Department of Homeland Security says

186
00:08:37,106 --> 00:08:39,866
current detection relies on random tips and

187
00:08:39,866 --> 00:08:42,433
laborious human intelligence collection.

188
00:08:42,883 --> 00:08:46,347
Agents send in robots and cameras, and scan

189
00:08:46,347 --> 00:08:47,797
floors with radar.

190
00:08:47,797 --> 00:08:50,859
But in 2025, the DHS inspector general

191
00:08:50,859 --> 00:08:53,598
reported that new tunnel detection

192
00:08:53,598 --> 00:08:56,579
technologies were still being tested.

193
00:08:57,029 --> 00:08:58,674
The law has caught up.

194
00:08:58,674 --> 00:09:01,291
Since 2006, building or financing a

195
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:04,207
cross-border tunnel is a federal crime,

196
00:09:04,207 --> 00:09:06,376
punishable by up to 20 years.

197
00:09:06,376 --> 00:09:09,666
Using one to smuggle doubles the maximum for

198
00:09:09,666 --> 00:09:11,237
the underlying crime.

199
00:09:11,687 --> 00:09:15,093
In March 2020, agents find a tunnel more than

200
00:09:15,093 --> 00:09:19,030
2,000 feet long, with its exit on Otay Center Drive.

201
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:22,512
For the first time in a San Diego tunnel, they

202
00:09:22,512 --> 00:09:24,557
seize five different drugs.

203
00:09:24,557 --> 00:09:27,812
Cocaine, marijuana, methamphetamine, heroin

204
00:09:27,812 --> 00:09:28,796
and fentanyl.

205
00:09:29,246 --> 00:09:29,730
The U.S.

206
00:09:29,730 --> 00:09:31,366
attorney at the time warns:

207
00:09:31,366 --> 00:09:34,091
“They can dig tunnels, but we will find them,

208
00:09:34,091 --> 00:09:36,755
fill them in and put the leaders in prison.”

209
00:09:37,205 --> 00:09:40,679
In May 2022, investigators watching a stash

210
00:09:40,679 --> 00:09:44,071
house in National City trace a tunnel to a

211
00:09:44,071 --> 00:09:47,544
warehouse in Otay Mesa, about 300 feet from

212
00:09:47,544 --> 00:09:48,917
the border fence.

213
00:09:49,367 --> 00:09:53,655
It's 1,744 feet long and 61 feet deep, with

214
00:09:53,655 --> 00:09:57,643
reinforced walls, rails, electricity and

215
00:09:57,643 --> 00:09:58,839
ventilation.

216
00:09:59,289 --> 00:10:03,174
Agents seize 1,762 pounds of cocaine, along

217
00:10:03,174 --> 00:10:06,065
with methamphetamine and heroin.

218
00:10:06,065 --> 00:10:08,143
Six people are charged.

219
00:10:08,593 --> 00:10:09,086
The U.S.

220
00:10:09,086 --> 00:10:10,258
attorney's verdict.

221
00:10:10,258 --> 00:10:12,849
“There is no more light at the end of this

222
00:10:12,849 --> 00:10:13,713
narco-tunnel.”

223
00:10:14,163 --> 00:10:16,641
And in May 2026, there's another.

224
00:10:16,641 --> 00:10:19,570
Its exit is hidden under the floor of a

225
00:10:19,570 --> 00:10:22,949
storage room, in what prosecutors describe as

226
00:10:22,949 --> 00:10:26,103
a supposed retail store near the Otay Mesa

227
00:10:26,103 --> 00:10:27,155
port of entry.

228
00:10:27,605 --> 00:10:30,510
Agents seize more than a ton of cocaine.

229
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:32,253
Four people are charged.

230
00:10:32,253 --> 00:10:35,376
Homeland Security Investigations calls it a

231
00:10:35,376 --> 00:10:38,717
significant blow to the Jalisco New Generation

232
00:10:38,717 --> 00:10:39,225
Cartel.

233
00:10:39,225 --> 00:10:41,259
The charges are allegations.

234
00:10:41,259 --> 00:10:43,946
The defendants are presumed innocent.

235
00:10:44,396 --> 00:10:47,927
By the Justice Department's count, 99 tunnels

236
00:10:47,927 --> 00:10:50,986
and passages have now been found in the

237
00:10:50,986 --> 00:10:54,360
Southern District of California since 1993.

238
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:56,321
28 of them sophisticated.

239
00:10:56,771 --> 00:10:57,788
The current U.S.

240
00:10:57,788 --> 00:10:59,694
attorney has a line ready too.

241
00:10:59,694 --> 00:11:02,426
“For these defendants, it wasn't a light at

242
00:11:02,426 --> 00:11:03,823
the end of the tunnel.

243
00:11:03,823 --> 00:11:05,475
It was lights and sirens.”

244
00:11:06,475 --> 00:11:09,682
In 36 years, the tunnels have gone from 200

245
00:11:09,682 --> 00:11:12,814
feet under a pool table to more than 4,000

246
00:11:12,814 --> 00:11:15,051
feet under an industrial park.

247
00:11:15,501 --> 00:11:17,680
Every one that's found gets sealed.

248
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,045
Every few years, another one turns up.

249
00:11:20,495 --> 00:11:22,612
The border fence stops at the ground.

250
00:11:22,612 --> 00:11:24,271
The smugglers start below it.

251
00:11:25,071 --> 00:11:26,980
Case file 002. Closed.

252
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:30,191
The next file is already on the desk.
